[list]
[*]A stand's work-type list now tells you when there is nothing in it, instead of showing an empty panel under the heading. Mods that rearrange work categories can take every entry out of it: Personal Work Categories switches a category off as soon as its preset has no work givers left in that column, and the same category leaves RimWorld's own Work tab at that moment. The blank panel read as this window having failed, which is the wrong place to go looking.
[*]That is also the check to run if categories go missing one at a time. Open the Work tab: a category that is gone from there as well was hidden by a work-category mod, and the stand list is reporting the game rather than losing track of it. Complex Jobs on its own does not do this, and neither does XML Extensions; both move work between categories without emptying any of them.
[*]Nothing about which work a stand serves has changed. A stand whose list you set by hand keeps the list you gave it, stands left on automatic still follow their room, and a category that returns to the Work tab returns here with it.
[*]The mod description, several tooltips and the workshop page were rewritten to one voice, and three claims in them were wrong. The decency guard ships switched off rather than holding garments back until you allow them, Anomaly is where vanilla's only lab coat comes from, and Deposit only is the setting that parks armor on a stand that hands out nothing in return.
[/list]
